# What the image build must not receive (`ENC-993`).
#
# `target/` alone is 29 GB on a developer machine — sending it as build context would cost more
# than the compile it is meant to save, and it cannot be reused anyway: the builder stage is a
# different libc, a different toolchain layout and, since `ENC-979`, a different profile
# fingerprint. The build inside the image starts cold on purpose.
#
# The exclusions below are ordered by what they cost if forgotten rather than alphabetically.

# Build output — the 29 GB one.
target/
web/dist/
web/node_modules/

# Version control and CI. The build reads no git metadata; `--locked` is what pins the inputs.
.git/
.github/

# Secrets and local configuration. `deploy/config/dev-keys/` holds development JWT signing keys
# generated on first run, and `enclave.yaml` is git-ignored precisely because it is the file an
# operator fills in with references to real ones. Neither is tracked, so neither would reach a
# commit — but the build context is not the index, and `COPY . .` does not consult `.gitignore`.
deploy/config/dev-keys/
enclave.yaml
*.pem
*.key

# Staged artefacts. `docs/11 §3.2` mounts all three at run time and this image deliberately
# contains none of them; a developer who staged them under the workspace must not have them
# silently baked in by a `COPY`, which is the licensing failure that section is written about.
**/embedding-model/
**/ocr-models/
**/pdfium/

# Scratch and editor state.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
opencalc/
